(O6010 SPINDLE TOOL WEAR + RUNOUT CHECK - REV 4A 2026-10-15)
(SET THE THREE VALUES BELOW FOR THE TOOL IN THE SPINDLE, THEN)
(CYCLE START IN MEMORY MODE. RUNS O6009 ON THE SPINDLE TOOL.)
(REV 4: FRONT END FOR O6009. THE OLD V3 MEASURED EVERY TOOL AS A)
(FLAT MILL 0.08-0.5MM ABOVE THE TIP AND READ THE DIAMETER FROM)
(#13000+T, NOW ALWAYS 0. ON A 4 FLUTE BALL ONLY 2 FLUTES REACH)
(THE TIP, SO THE EDGE CHECK SAW 2 OF 4 PULSES - ALARM 15)
(CUTTING EDGE BROKEN. K-1 MEASURES A BALL AT ITS EQUATOR WHERE)
(ALL FLUTES ARE FULL DIAMETER.)
(C MUST BE THE FLUTE COUNT AT THE MEASURING HEIGHT.)
(WRITES THE MEASURED DIAMETER CHANGE TO #12000+T.)
(RUN STANDALONE ONLY. FROM ANOTHER PROGRAM CALL O6009 DIRECTLY -)
(G65 P6010 WOULD EXCEED THE C00 LIMIT OF 4 NESTED G65 CALLS.)
#1 = 1.5875 (D - NOMINAL DIAMETER MM. 1/16 IN = 1.5875)
#2 = 4. (C - NUMBER OF FLUTES. MUST BE EXACT)
#3 = -1. (K - 0 FLAT, -1 BALL, CORNER RADIUS MM = BULLNOSE, -3 DRILL)
G65 P6009 T#3700 D#1 C#2 K#3
M30
